      "message": "Hi Yongqin, thanks for pointing this out.  Just for the sake of reproducibility, which SHA where you on?\n\nThe warning we first see in [1] as shared by Yongqin above, is caused by the fact that the buffer head\u0027s count is less than 1 inside of __sync_dirty_buffer(): https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android12-5.10/fs/buffer.c#3189 .  According to the description of the funciton, the caller is expected to hold a reference, so it is likely that my patch is decrementing the reference of a buffer head when that should not be the case.  I will compare the original version of the patch created by Laura (http://patches.linaro.org/patch/11327/), which should be stable, with the one submitted here - I will provide further updates accordingly.",
